From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:42:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: pace J604 panel video onto the 120 Hz
 grid by default

The J604 panel shows each swap at the next tick of a 4.17 ms grid, on
either phase of its 120 Hz refresh. Chromium times its frames from the
presentation times and, with frames landing on both phases, presented a
60 fps video with about 40 % of its frames 12.5 or 20.9 ms apart, and a
24 fps one with about 30 % off its 41.7 ms cadence; mpv paced itself.

With swap_pace on (held only at video rates, with the learned floor),
measured on the J604: 60 fps video 97 to 100 % of frames 16.67 ms apart
(requestVideoFrameCallback p5/p95 16.6/16.8 ms), 30 fps p5/p95 33.3/33.4,
24 fps p5/p95 41.6/41.8, mpv 100 %; a 120 fps animation and scrolling
unchanged at 120 fps, all frames on the grid.

Turn swap_pace on by default. swap_pace=0 restores the previous
behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 9a6e1c207d27ef1d31837ed13edf7bfa4b884bbe)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index cca0a312bd..1880d51f53 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -185,10 +185,10 @@ module_param(swap_target_lead_us, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(swap_target_lead_us,
 		 "J604: with swap_target=2, how far ahead of submission the target tick must be, us (default 2000)");
 
-static bool swap_pace;
+static bool swap_pace = true;
 module_param(swap_pace, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(swap_pace,
-		 "J604: before an internal-panel swap, wait when the frame would otherwise be shown on the panel tick between two 120 Hz refreshes (4.17 ms after one), so it is shown on the 120 Hz grid of the last completion (experimental; default: off)");
+		 "J604: at video rates, wait before an internal-panel swap when the frame would otherwise be shown on the panel tick between two 120 Hz refreshes (4.17 ms after one), so video is shown on the 120 Hz grid of the last completion (default: on)");
 
 static unsigned int swap_pace_min_us = 14600;
 module_param(swap_pace_min_us, uint, 0644);
